    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DC20BB66F0C9CF9F562615950604C1D5/jobs/89717": {
      "title": "Adjunct- Dance for the Actor",
      "description": "Adjunct- Dance for the Actor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct- Dance for the Actor DES MOINES, IA 50316 Apply Apply Description The Theatre Arts Department at Grand View University seeks an experienced dance instructor to teach Dance for the Actor , an introductory dance course designed specifically for theatre students. The course introduces students to fundamental dance technique, terminology, movement, and physical awareness with an emphasis on skills applicable to musical theatre and stage performance . Students will develop basic dance vocabulary, coordination, rhythm, flexibility, strength, and confidence while learning to apply movement skills to theatrical performance. The ideal candidate will have professional or academic experience in dance and a strong interest in working with beginning-level performers. Experience teaching dance to actors, musical theatre performers, or young people is highly desirable. Responsibilities The successful candidate will: Teach an introductory Dance for the Actor course for undergraduate theatre students. Introduce students to basic dance vocabulary, terminology, and technique. Develop students' coordination, musicality, rhythm, physical awareness, and movement confidence. Incorporate foundational styles and movement commonly encountered in musical theatre. Provide instruction appropriate for students with varied levels of previous dance experience. Help students develop the physical skills and vocabulary necessary for participation in musical theatre productions and auditions. Create a positive, inclusive, and supportive learning environment. Prepare and deliver lessons, demonstrations, exercises, and choreography appropriate to beginning-level performers. Evaluate student progress and provide constructive feedback. Follow university policies and course expectations related to instruction, grading, and attendance Please include the following with your application: Current Resume Contact information for 3 references Unofficial transcript All applicants must apply through our online application system. Pre-employment background check required. Qualifications Required: •    Bachelor's degree (BA or equivalent). •    Demonstrated dance training and performance experience. •    Previous teaching or instructional experience in dance, theatre, musical theatre, or a related performing arts discipline. •    Ability to teach beginning-level dance students in a supportive and accessible manner. Preferred: •    MFA, MA, or other graduate degree in Dance, Theatre, Musical Theatre, or a related field. •    Experience teaching dance specifically to actors or musical theatre students. •    Professional experience in musical theatre performance or choreography. •    Experience with multiple dance styles commonly used in musical theatre. •    College-level teaching experience. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DC20BB66F0C9CF9F562615950604C1D5/jobs/89711": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Education or Professor of Practice I",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Education or Professor of Practice I You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor of Education or Professor of Practice I DES MOINES, IA 50316 Apply Apply Description POSITION: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF EDUCATION (TENURE TRACK) or PROFESSOR OF PRACTICE I EFFECTIVE DATE: Fall 2027 Overview: The Education Department at Grand View University in Des Moines, Iowa, invites applications from candidates who are excited to join an innovative department within a liberal arts setting offering undergraduate and Master’s degree programs. Our department is committed to strengthening the teaching profession through intentional recruitment, support and retention of future educators. We prepare teachers to recognize and respond to barriers to educational access, support and retention of future educators. We prepare teachers to recognize and respond to barriers to educational access, understand the ways schools and educators can contribute to positive change, and created learning environments in which all students can thrive. Grand View University is proud to be a student-ready institution that serves a significant population of first-generation college students, transfer students, and students with a wide range of educational and life experiences. Our faculty work closely with students to foster belonging, academic success, professional growth and meaning engagement in their communities. Successful candidates will contribute to strengthening our elementary and secondary education programs, with expertise in literacy (Science of Reading or Dyslexia) or social sciences teaching. Candidates should demonstrate a commitment to excellence and innovation in undergraduate and/or graduate teaching to working collaboratively with traditional and non-traditional students in a small-college environment. We seek faculty who are committed to student success, engage actively in scholarly and/or professional activities, and bring relevant perspectives and experiences to their work with candidates. Responsibilities: Candidate will be expected to teach a range of courses in a variety of modalities, including in person, blended and online. Academic responsibilities include: teaching, developing undergraduate and graduate courses, supervising pre-service or in-service teachers, staying current in the field, maintaining an appropriate scholarly agenda, and advising students. Candidate will be expected to provide additional service to the University, educational profession, and the community at large Candidates will be expected to support the University and Department mission. Department Mission: Grand View’s Teacher Education Program empowers teachers, through vibrant learning communities and self-reflection, to be innovative, culturally responsive, and resourceful leaders, who are empowered to respond to the dynamic needs of learners for a global society. Grand View’s Commitment to You: Grand View provides an intentional mentoring and support program through our Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning (CETL). New faculty are paired with experienced faculty as a component of an intentional induction program. Faculty in the Education Department collaborate on a regular basis to ensure that the program is preparing teacher candidates to engage in the K-12 schools of the 21st century as innovative, culturally responsive advocates for their students and colleagues. Application: Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026. Position will remain open until filled. Application will need to include the following information: Curriculum Vitae, including names and contact information for three references A letter of application that includes: Why you are a unique and good fit Information about your scholarly agenda Experiences that address the above minimum and desired/preferred qualifications Teaching Statement which includes Approach to mentoring pre-service and novice teachers Describe your teaching philosophy Copies of all transcripts that include relevant coursework All applicants should submit their materials through our online application process. Pre-employment background check required. Qualifications Job Qualifications Master's of Education (Professor of Practice I candidates) with a willingness to pursue a terminal degree Minimum 3 years of successful teaching experience in K-12 setting. Preferred Qualifications: Prefer candidates with elementary or secondary experience; the ideal candidate has taught K-12 with Social Sciences teaching or Literacy (Dyslexia or Science of Reading) expertise. Prior successful teaching at the post-secondary level. Supervision/mentoring experience of pre-service or novice teachers is desired. Earned Ph.D./ Ed.D. degree in Education (Assistant Professor, tenure-track candidates), ABD will be considered. Candidates are preferred to have at least five years of successful teaching experience at the K-12 level. Educational leadership or school administration experience preferred. Experience and passion for mentoring, recruitment and retention, and collaboration with local schools and education stakeholders. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DC20BB66F0C9CF9F562615950604C1D5/jobs/89250": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor or Professor of Practice I Mathematics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor or Professor of Practice I Mathematics You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor or Professor of Practice I Mathematics DES MOINES, IA 50316 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply Assistant Professor or Professor of Practice I Mathematics Fall Semester 2027 Tenure Track The candidate will be responsible to teach all of our Math Education courses, for both Elementary and Secondary teaching students. To round out the teaching load expectations, the candidate will also need to be able to teach other math courses. These additional courses will be ones best suited for the individual and can range from non-major service courses to upper-division courses for Applied Mathematics majors. The ideal candidate will be able supervise practicum and/or student teachers in Math. The candidate will be expected to support the mission of the University. Other duties include active involvement in activities to stay current in their field, maintaining an appropriate scholarly agenda, advising students, and University, professional and public service. There is also opportunity to teach service courses and contribute to the general education core beyond Math courses. APPLICATION: Review of applications will begin December 8, 2026 . Position will remain open until filled. All applications must include a letter of application, curriculum vitae, statements of teaching philosophy and scholarly interests that address the above minimum and desired/preferred qualifications, and copies of all transcripts that include relevant course work. Three to five reference names must be provided, at least two that can speak about teaching abilities. All applicants should submit their materials through our online application process. Pre-employment background check required. Qualifications MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Master’s in Mathematics Education, Mathematics, or similar field with preference of Ph.D. Rank determined by experience and credentials. Tenure track position for Ph.D. candidates and Professor of Practice position for non-Ph.D. candidates. DESIRED/PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: a commitment to teaching excellence, including prior successful teaching of Math Education courses, an active program of scholarship appropriate for a Liberal Arts institution, and a commitment to the mission of Grand View University. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DC20BB66F0C9CF9F562615950604C1D5/jobs/86922": {
      "title": "Theatre Designer/Technical Director",
      "description": "Theatre Designer/Technical Director You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Theatre Designer/Technical Director DES MOINES, IA 50316 Apply Apply Description This 9-month Designer/Technical Director Position is responsible for designing and mentoring students through four productions each year in the areas of scenic, lighting and sound. Additionally, this position is responsible for scheduling, managing and overseeing all technical elements in the Viking theatre, including theatre productions and theatre rentals. The Designer/Technical Director will also manage and mentor work-study students who work in the shops and stage crews for productions. Degree in a Design area with Technical Direction experience or degree in Technical Direction with Design experience is necessary. A collaborative spirit and strong organizational skills are highly desirable. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to teach design and technical courses for additional compensation according to their expertise. Position runs Mid- August through Mid-May. Degree in design with technical theatre experience or degree in technical theatre with design experience required. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF JOB Design, or mentor student designers, in areas of scenic, lighting and sound Schedule, manage and oversee all technical (scenic, lighting and sound) elements for theatre production Collaborate with the conferencing manager to schedule and oversee manage all technical elements for external events held in the theatre Maintain and improve scene shop, control booth light shop, and theatre storage areas Hold regular shop hours and mentor student workers in technical theatre Maintain a safe work environment for student workers and theatrical participants Order supplies for theatre productions and maintain stock of essential supplies in shops Maintain financial records and budgets for productions WORKING CONDITIONS Irregular hours- weekends and nights as needed Use of power tools Lifting large and heavy objects and scenic elements Climbing ladders and scaffolding Climbing up to and bending down on the grid This position is an 9-month position from mid-August through mid-May and will have irregular hours based upon theatre production schedule. Time off for Christmas Break, Thanksgiving Break and Spring Break. Interested candidates should apply via our online application process and include a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three references. Pre-employment background check required. Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS and REQUIREMENTS Scenic Design and Construction Lighting Design and electrics, board operation Working knowledge of basic soundboard mixing and Q-lab. Ability to work on a deadline, according to the production calendar Ability to mentor and inspire students who are new to theatre Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
