    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DC20BB66F0C9CF9F562615950604C1D5/jobs/86890": {
      "title": "Part Time Clinical Nursing Lab Assistant",
      "description": "Part Time Clinical Nursing Lab Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Part Time Clinical Nursing Lab Assistant DES MOINES, IA 50316 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Education Level 2 Year Degree Category Other Apply Description Grand View University is seeking a part-time Nursing Lab Assistant to support the Nursing Education Department's Center for Learning.  This position provides hands-on operational support for nursing skills labs, including preparing laboratory spaces, maintaining supplies and equipment that will support students' skill development, training, and assisting faculty and the Simulation Educator. This is an academic-year, part-time position averaging approximately 20 hours per week . Work hours will vary based on course schedules, lab activities, and department needs and will generally be scheduled between 7:00 a.m. and 3:00 p.m. The position follows the academic calendar and includes work surrounding the start of each semester through finals week. Essential Responsibilities Clinical Lab Preparation and Support Prepare and reset clinical lab spaces for Foundations and Assessment courses, including set-up and tear-down of equipment, supplies, and learning materials. Help ensure lab spaces are organized, stocked, clean, and ready for scheduled student learning activities. Provide open-lab opportunities and support for students referred to the Center for Learning for skills practice or remediation. Assist the Simulation Educator with lab and simulation activities as needed. Center for Learning Operations Support the day-to-day organization and readiness of the Center for Learning during scheduled work hours. Maintain inventory and catalog new supplies, purchases, and equipment. Prepare and coordinate supply tote orders for Foundations courses. Research, source, and order clinical lab supplies and equipment. Assist with equipment evaluation, purchasing, routine maintenance, repair coordination, and replacement needs. Research equipment options in response to faculty and departmental lab needs. Maintain appropriate supplies of gowns, bedding, towels, and other reusable materials and coordinate laundry exchanges. Administrative and Department Support Assist the Department Chair with monitoring and managing the Center for Learning budget. Maintain accurate records related to supplies, equipment, purchasing, and inventory. Participate in Nursing Education Department meetings as appropriate. Provide tours and hands-on experiences for prospective students, visitors, and other groups. Perform other Center for Learning and clinical lab support duties as needed. Schedule Part-time, approximately 20 hours per week Hours will vary based on the Nursing Education Department’s course, lab, and student-support needs Work will generally occur between 7:00 a.m. and 3:00 p.m. Some weeks or days may require different hours based on scheduled clinical labs, student remediation, special events, or department priorities Position follows the academic calendar , with work beginning around back-to-school activities and continuing through finals week each semester Qualifications Mininimum Job Requirements Medical certification in CNA, CMA, EMT, RT, or related field Associates degree Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DC20BB66F0C9CF9F562615950604C1D5/jobs/86006": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Chemistry/Biochemistry",
      "description": "Assistant Professor Chemistry/Biochemistry You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor Chemistry/Biochemistry DES MOINES, IA 50316 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply Description Tenure Track Duties: The successful candidate will be expected to develop and teach a range of courses including those designed primarily for Biochemistry majors (e.g. Biochemistry, Biochemical Techniques), foundation courses for Biochemistry, Biology and Nursing majors (e.g. General Chemistry, Fundamentals of Organic and Biochemistry), and courses in the general education core. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to inclusive and culturally responsive pedagogy and a commitment to continued growth in these practices. In addition, the successful candidate will work with department members to develop, provide and/or coordinate on-campus and off-campus undergraduate research experiences for students. Other duties include advising a diverse population of students, and participating in activities that serve the Department, University and community. Application: To be considered for the position, candidates must submit the following: Letter of application Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy and research interests Copies of all transcripts (unofficial transcripts are satisfactory at this time) Complete contact information for three references All applicants must apply through our online application system. A pre-employment background check is required. Preferred appointment start date is January 2027.   Priority deadline for applications is October 1, 2026. Applicants with availability for a Fall 2027 start date are encouraged to apply and will receive full consideration. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Biochemistry, Chemistry, or related field with training or research experience in the area of biochemistry. Desired/Preferred Qualifications: Prefer prior teaching experience working with traditional students as well as non-traditional students. Postdoctoral research experience and an interest in mentoring undergraduate students in research are desirable. Preference will be given to candidates who are able to teach all levels of undergraduate biochemistry and general chemistry. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DC20BB66F0C9CF9F562615950604C1D5/jobs/85045": {
      "title": "Admissions Assistant",
      "description": "Admissions Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Admissions Assistant DES MOINES, IA 50316 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply Description General Purpose of Job: The Admission Assistant will greet prospective students and their families to Grand View University admissions office, coordinate all details of the prospective student’s visit and gather detailed and implicit information from web and phone inquiries.  They will also appropriately direct phone and personal inquiries to various members of the campus community, always maintain an impeccable professional manner at front desk when dealing with the public, internal faculty, and staff. Essential Functions of Job: Render hospitality plan for all campus visitors with a welcoming, positive attitude at all times. Answer admissions telephone and direct callers to the appropriate individual.  Responsible for initiating phone system maintenance and service calls for all admission trunk numbers.  Coordinate messages on the answering machine as well as update recording as required. Screen and distribute Admissions staff mail and emails when appropriate. Assist with creating all applicant files in SLATE. Receive and stamp transcripts for Data Team. Oversee campus visit appointment book for prospective students and maintain an accurate record of visitors in the appointment book daily.  Help assist Admissions Counselor who is directly in charge of managing the tour guides. Assist with using scheduler to add visiting students in SLATE calendar and checking them in via scheduler (arrived or concluded). In charge of ordering office supplies via Triplett. Keep parking passes. Set individualized campus tours in SLATE for prospective families by emailing appropriate faculty and staff and/or coach and coordinating the timeline for each visit. Maintain itinerary of Admissions Counselors and the Director of Undergraduate Admissions. Train new admissions staff in front desk procedures (opening mail, creating applicant files, telephone procedures, etc.) Pull and print web inquiries daily. Pull and print, or electronically distribute inquiries, readmit applications, information requests, RSVP’s, etc. from the general admissions email account . Create welcome sheets and welcome list for visiting students daily. Look through mail.  Admissions return mail goes to data team, all other mail gets distributed according to department. Manage copy projects, delivery of paperwork to other offices, etc. in a timely manner. Assemble visitor packets as needed, working with student ambassadors.  Must make sure there is inventory of sheets for packets, request orders from database manager when low. As an agent of the University, this position is expected to represent the college as a trained professional.  Appropriate dress and demeanor are essential as is always courtesy and superb customer services to prospective students, parents, current students, faculty, staff and other members of the college community. Manage vehicle usage and car reservations Email list of visitors of the day to Marketing daily. Send outlook calendar invites to faculty, coaches & counselors. For virtual meetings, you must be comfortable with using Microsoft Teams. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of Undergraduate Admissions. Working Conditions: Position hours are Monday - Friday 8:00am - 4:00pm Work is performed in a normal office setting. Sits, stands, bends, lifts and moves intermittently during working hours. During course of day, you may be interacting with students, faculty and staff by computer, phone or in person. Qualifications Word Processing Skills Ability to work in a fast-paced environment, working on multiple tasks with minimal supervision. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DC20BB66F0C9CF9F562615950604C1D5/jobs/82060": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant - Strength and Conditioning",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant - Strength and Conditioning You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Graduate Assistant - Strength and Conditioning DES MOINES, IA 50316 Apply Apply Description Grand View (NAIA – IA): Grand View University Strength and Conditioning Department is accepting applications for a Graduate Assistant Position (tuition waiver + stipend). Responsibilities include, but are not limited to, assisting with all sports and the opportunity to lead 2-3 teams. Hours will vary and will include early mornings and late evenings, and some travel. Other responsibilities include: assisting with supervision and execution of strength training programs for various sports, daily maintenance and upkeep of facility, completing an ongoing curriculum. Candidates will receive valuable hands-on coaching experience in all aspects as well as the opportunity to learn and grow in the field of Strength & Conditioning. Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS: Candidates must hold a BA/BS in Kinesiology or Exercise Science related field. CPR, First Aid and AED certification required. Possess or be working toward CSCS through the NSCA or the SCCC through the CSCCa. Candidates must possess strong communication skills, positive energy, attention to detail, sense of urgency, and strong work ethic. Skills and proficiency with Microsoft Excel, Teambuildr, GymAware, and OVR is recommended. All applicants must apply through our online application system and should include a cover letter, resume, and references. A pre-employment background check is required. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DC20BB66F0C9CF9F562615950604C1D5/jobs/81941": {
      "title": "Part Time Adjunct-English",
      "description": "Part Time Adjunct-English You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Part Time Adjunct-English DES MOINES, IA 50316 Apply Apply Description The Department of English at Grand View University is seeking part-time instructors to teach a range of writing and literature courses. Most of the courses are traditional, face-to-face, day classes, but there are occasional opportunities to teach evening or online courses as well. Courses includes (but are not limited to):  he Department of English at Grand View University is seeking part-time instructors to teach a range of writing and literature courses. The majority of the courses are traditional, day classes, but there are occasional opportunities to teach evening or online courses as well. Courses includes (but are not limited to): ENGL 100: English Literacies: This course focuses on the development of functional literacy skills- reading and writing- and helps students advance both for the needs of university work. ENGL 101: First Year Composition: This course emphasizes the process model of writing, argument structure, and research. ENGL 111: Interpretation of Literature: This course focuses on helping students enjoy, analyze, and communicate their interpretations of a range of literary genres. ENGL 212: Good & Evil: This course is thematic and focuses on core ethical and philosophical questions about the nature of good and evil. ENGL 309: Writing for Business: This advanced writing course focuses on the rhetoric of business reports through analysis of audience, context, and purpose. The Department prides itself on opportunities for instructors to develop their teaching through course design. We also offer mentoring and professional development opportunities for all instructors. Candidates should have teaching experience and hold a master’s degree in English or related field (PhD preferred). The English Department is dedicated to linguistic justice and student success. The ideal candidate will abide by and uphold these core values in their teaching and scholarship. This is a continuous job posting to establish a qualified pool of part-time instructors on an as-needed basis semester-to-semester. APPLICATION: Review of applications will begin immediately. All applications must include a letter of application, curriculum vitae or resume, and contact information for 3 references. All applicants must apply through our online application system. A pre-employment background check is required. Qualifications Master's degree in English or a related field required (PhD preferred). Teaching experience in higher education. Strong writing skills and the ability to communicate effectively with students. Experience working with diverse populations. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Experience in teaching online or evening courses. Familiarity with diverse teaching methodologies. Commitment to inclusive teaching practices. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DC20BB66F0C9CF9F562615950604C1D5/jobs/81933": {
      "title": "Part Time Adjunct - Music (Fall 2026)",
      "description": "Part Time Adjunct - Music (Fall 2026) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Part Time Adjunct - Music (Fall 2026) DES MOINES, IA 50316 Apply Apply Description Music Adjunct and Lesson Instructors The Department of Music at Grand View University accepts applications for part-time music faculty. Duties may include private lesson instruction, leading music ensembles, or general education courses including music appreciation, fundamentals of music, and musics of the world. Courses and lessons are face-to-face. We have an immediate need for Fundamentals of Music for Fall 2026. We offer private instruction in: Voice, Piano, Guitar, Brass, Woodwinds, Percussion, and Strings. This is a continuous job posting to establish a qualified pool of part-time instructors on an as-needed basis semester-to-semester.   All applicants on file will be kept should needs in these areas arise. Application Review of applications will begin immediately. All applications must include a letter of application, curriculum vitae or resume, and contact information for 3 references. All applicants must apply through our online application system. A pre-employment background check is required. Qualifications Master's degree in Music or a related field required (PhD preferred). Teaching experience in higher education preferred. Strong communion skills, Experience working with diverse populations. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DC20BB66F0C9CF9F562615950604C1D5/jobs/55958": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant - Women's Soccer",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant - Women's Soccer You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Graduate Assistant - Women's Soccer DES MOINES, IA 50316 Apply Apply Description Grand View (Des Moines, IA): Grand View University Athletics Department is accepting applications for a Women’s Soccer - Graduate Assistant position (tuition waiver + stipend) starting Fall 2026 semester. SUPERVISED BY: Head Coach & Assistant Coach Selected Candidate will receive valuable hands-on coaching experience in all aspects of coaching, as well as the opportunity to learn and grow in the sport of Soccer. RESPONSIBILITIES: Assist Women’s Soccer staff in all aspects of training. Be an example to student athletes in professional conduct, sportsmanship, teamwork and academic excellence. Attend all games and training dates. Manage Soccer Equipment Support the academic success of reserve players to ensure eligibility, retention, and graduation. Assist in program logistics including transportation, travel, meals, transportation, inventory and lodging. Obrain and distribute parking passes for off-campus players on away games. Helping to set up the field on game days and tearing it down Keep Athletic Trainers and other coaching staff updated with observed injuries or fatigue. Assist in scheduling and recruiting Assist in marketing and branding efforts including social media Video recruiting analysis and recruiting duties, as assigned Fostering and building good mentor relations with players. Promote a positive and disciplined team culture that aligns with Grand View University values and university standards. Wear practice and game attire appropriate for coaching staff. Perform other related duties as assigned by the Head Coach and Assistant Coach In Season (August - December) Assist Women’s Soccer Coaching Staff in preparation for pre-season team camp Prepare soccer equipment for variety and reserve teams’ practices Manage the Varsity Reserve program Designing and implementing specific practice sessions Evaluate and meet with each reserve team player Off Season (January – May) Work through recruiting lists Assist with Winter and Summer Camps All applicants must apply through our online application system. A pre-employment background check is required. Qualifications Candidates must hold a BA/BS degree.  Degrees in Sports Management, Coaching, Kinesiology, Exercise Science, or related field are preferred Collegiate playing and/or coaching experience preferred CPR, First Aid and AED certification required Must complete NAIA Coaching Modules Ability to work well in a team environment Good character & communication skills, self-motivation, and leadership skills are essential. Strong organizational and time management skills The ideal candidate will have a strong desire to be a collegiate coach and will possess a strong work ethic, high character values, attention to detail, sense of urgency, and a willingness to learn and grow Skills and proficiency with Microsoft Excel, Teambuildr, Hudl is preferred Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DC20BB66F0C9CF9F562615950604C1D5/jobs/45462": {
      "title": "Adjunct - Business",
      "description": "Adjunct - Business You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct - Business DES MOINES, IA 50316 Apply Apply Description Part-Time Faculty for Business Subject Areas The Department of Business is seeking qualified applicants for part-time faculty positions. Please contact Dr. Shannon Juergens with any questions: sjuergens@grandview.edu Qualifications Previous teaching experience and relevant experience in the subject area are desired. Business subject areas may include accounting, business, finance, investments, operations, information systems, statistics, marketing, sales, sport management, economics, human resource management, business law, and other related fields. Master's degree in the content area required, PhD preferred. Application: Please include letter of application, vita/resume, cover letter, transcripts (unofficial satisfactory at this time) and contact information for three references in your online application materials. All applicants must apply through our online application system. A pre-employment background check is required. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DC20BB66F0C9CF9F562615950604C1D5/jobs/36772": {
      "title": "Art Adjunct",
      "description": "Art Adjunct You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Art Adjunct DES MOINES, IA 50316 Apply Apply Description Grand View University Art Adjunct In addition to its regular, full-time faculty, we seek faculty and creative professionals with industry experience to teach courses on a part-time basis. These positions are not available every semester and are contingent upon course offerings. Qualifications To be qualified to teach at the university, candidates must possess a terminal degree in studio art or graphic design. In occasional cases, demonstrated professional experience in a specialized discipline and a sustained history of distinguished professional work, compelling creative achievements, or other significant experience in the relevant field may be considered as an alternative to the required degree. Required Master's degree in Fine Arts or related field, or a significant record of accomplishment in the field Excellent communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills Ability to translate complex art concepts into clear, accessible assignments Preferred Master of Fine Art degree in Studio Art, Printmaking, Sculpture, Graphic Design, Photography or related discipline Demonstrated success in teaching, lecturing, or mentoring students, either in an academic or professional setting, in higher education studio art or design programs A passion for teaching and a commitment to fostering a learning environment that encourages creativity, critical thinking, and professional growth among students Experience working in various studio art contexts Ability to engage students effectively convey concepts, critique, and guide students in developing their portfolios An understanding of current trends in the art field to provide insights into the evolving nature of the field To Apply Submit a cover letter, resume, online portfolio link or PDF of sample of creative/professional work and contact information for at least three references. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DC20BB66F0C9CF9F562615950604C1D5/jobs/20652": {
      "title": "Adjunct - Clinical Nursing",
      "description": "Adjunct - Clinical Nursing You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct - Clinical Nursing DES MOINES, IA 50316 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Apply Description Part-Time Adjunct Nursing Clinical Faculty Responsibilities : The adjunct clinical faculty will be responsible to the Department Chair of Nursing and the Nursing Faculty in the individual nursing course(s) for which they are assigned. Clinical teaching faculty will provide clinical instruction to a group or groups of nursing students. Limits on numbers of students are imposed by the Iowa Board of Nursing. Attend orientation sessions at Grand View as appropriate. Meet with the course instructor prior to the semester. Consult weekly with the course faculty. Provide weekly progression notes on students using the Student Progress Report. Negotiate with course faculty regarding course responsibilities and grading of assignments. Assist in evaluation of students using the Student Progress Report. Application: Review of applications will begin immediately. All applications must include a letter of application, curriculum vitae or resume, copy of current Iowa Nursing License, and contact information for 3 references. Qualifications Bachelor of Science in Nursing or Bachelor of Arts in Nursing or higher degree. Master’s Degree preferred, or must be working towards a Master’s Degree in nursing Two years of clinical experience in nursing. Current Iowa RN licensure (Individuals who are currently licensed in another state and recognized for licensure in Iowa, pursuant to the nurse licensure compact contained in Iowa code). Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DC20BB66F0C9CF9F562615950604C1D5/jobs/18723": {
      "title": "Adjunct Candidate Pool",
      "description": "Adjunct Candidate Pool You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Candidate Pool DES MOINES, IA 50316 Apply Apply Description Grand View University accepts applications for part-time faculty at any time. If there is not a specific part-time faculty opening posted on our website, candidates may submit their information to this posting.  We will share the application materials with the appropriate department for consideration when there is a need for an adjunct instructor. If you have previously applied for a posted adjunct opening in a specific area of discipline, you do not need to apply to this general posting.  Your previous application is kept with the appropriate department in case future part-time opportunities arise for which you are qualified.  You may update your materials at any time by logging into the application system with the email you originally used during application. Please include a cover letter indicating what courses/subjects you wish to teach. Previous teaching experience and relevant experience in the subject area are desired.  PhD preferred, master's degree in the content area required. In addition to the cover letter and vita/resume, please include transcripts (unofficial are satisfactory at this time), and three references. Applications will remain active for One-Year after submission. Pre-employment background check required. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DC20BB66F0C9CF9F562615950604C1D5/jobs/18010": {
      "title": "Adjunct - Psychology",
      "description": "Adjunct - Psychology You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct - Psychology DES MOINES, IA 50316 Apply Apply Description We are accepting applications for part-time faculty teaching within the Department of Psychology and Human Services. Please include letter of application, vita/resume, transcripts (unofficial satisfactory at this time) and contact information for three references in your online application materials. All applicants must apply through our website. A pre-employment background check is required. Qualifications Previous teaching experience and relevant experience in the subject area are desired. Ph.D. preferred, Master's degree in the content area required. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DC20BB66F0C9CF9F562615950604C1D5/jobs/15435": {
      "title": "Adjunct - Sociology",
      "description": "Adjunct - Sociology You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct - Sociology DES MOINES, IA 50316 Apply Apply Description Accepting applications for Sociology Adjunct Instructor Please include with your application: Letter of Interest Resume or CV Unofficial Transcript Contact Information for 3 References Qualifications PhD or JD preferred, Master's degree with significant coursework in family is required. All applicants must apply through our online system. A pre-employment background check is required. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DC20BB66F0C9CF9F562615950604C1D5/jobs/10972": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty and Practicum Supervisors for Education Department",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty and Practicum Supervisors for Education Department You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty and Practicum Supervisors for Education Department DES MOINES, IA 50316 Apply Apply Description The Grand View Practicum Supervisor has the responsibility for assisting, coaching, supervising, and evaluating the student teacher during the semester of student teaching. Supervisors are required to visit and observe every other week for each 8-week placement (students have 2 - placements). Supervisors must also participate in the mid-term evaluation and final evaluation conference with the student teacher and the cooperating teacher. Other responsibilities center on the assessment of the student teaching assignments. This posting is for the candidate pool for the Education Department. Each semester there are needs for Practicum Supervisors and Adjunct Lecturers. Semesters begin in August, January and May. Applications will remain active for 1-year after submission. You may update your application at any time. Qualifications Qualifications: Previous teaching experience and relevant experience in the subject area are desired. PhD preferred, Master's degree in the content area required. Specialist Endorsements preferred Please include letter of application, vita/resume, transcripts (unofficial satisfactory at this time) and contact information for three references in your online application materials. All applicants must apply through our online application system. A pre-employment background check is required. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DC20BB66F0C9CF9F562615950604C1D5/jobs/10762": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Social Work (BSW or MSW)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Social Work (BSW or MSW) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty - Social Work (BSW or MSW) DES MOINES, IA 50316 Apply Apply Description Seeking qualified candidates for Adjunct Lecturer positions for Master of Social Work and Bachelor of Social Work programs. Semesters begin in August, January and May. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Candidates must have a master’s degree in social work (MSW) from a CSWE-accredited program. Candidates must have at least two years post-master’s social work degree practice experience. DUTIES: The selected candidate will serve as an adjunct lecturer in the MSW and/or BSW program. APPLICATION: To be considered for the position, candidates must submit the following: Letter of introduction or Cover Letter Curriculum vitae or Resume Copies of all transcripts (unofficial transcripts are satisfactory at this time) Complete contact information for three references A pre-employment background check is required. Grand View University aspires to serve a varying, multi-faceted community of learners - students, faculty, and staff - in a welcoming environment so that each learner can achieve their fullest potential. Our objective is to foster and sustain a campus environment free from imbalance and/or bias, while also preparing students “called and empowered to serve the neighbor so that all may flourish.” At Grand View University, we adhere to the Lutheran tradition of being “ r ooted and open;” we value differing beliefs, backgrounds and perspectives and welcome and affirm the thoughts and experiences each distinct member brings to our community. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
